 raised roughly $2.4 million and holds $2.7 million on hand, dwarfing Democrat Raymond Smith Jr.'s $223,000 raised and $74,000 in cash. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nRatings from nine expert outlets lean heavily Republican, with five calling the seat Safe or Solid R. The only public poll, taken in early August by a Democratic-leaning firm, showed Murphy ahead just 44-41, a narrower spread than the district's fundamentals suggest. Markets price Murphy's chances near 86 percent. The seat remains very likely to stay Republican, with modest residual uncertainty from sparse polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0567, "margin": -10.0}]}